{"id": "EUVD-2026-80639", "enisaUuid": "3fb311d0-5a89-31dc-a124-87fe3cbcea33", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb-storage: ene_ub6250: fix race between scan work and probe\n\nene_ub6250_probe() calls usb_stor_probe2(), which starts the usb-storage\ninfrastructure and schedules the delayed scan work.  The driver then\ncalls ene_get_card_type(), which sends an ENE command through\nene_send_scsi_cmd() and the usb-storage bulk transfer helpers.\n\nBoth the delayed scan work, through usb_stor_Bulk_max_lun(), and\nene_get_card_type() use us->current_urb.  The scan work serializes this\naccess with us->dev_mutex, but the ENE card-type probe does not.  If the\nscan work runs while ene_get_card_type() is still using us->current_urb,\nusb_submit_urb() warns that the URB is already active.\n\nSerialize ene_get_card_type() with us->dev_mutex, matching the locking\nused by the scan path.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:33:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:56:48", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9cd335f4f41e84d1ab88d80150ffee8dee9650d7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8936d95dd04d34db96d4d1e3899eee52605bbedc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9c261a83131e241d67cb73ab578d0265bc19cfb5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9481bc04a8c351ed883a7f0e10939bbe9120ead7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5082546702c32a2700894d2c0ace784e038ef6a3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1c67f2ba9c5f7c5ab3670671c0d51c6504bcaf74", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/996c319b8bd5ada1f62daae0d331d0b23e0f2117", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/445fc368c6bc73eff0aeb3818cf5f355facfbb16"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5fv5-xjmm-vvx9", "CVE-2026-90031"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "17c978f4-536b-3410-bef0-e27b716624fd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "1a97e978-f781-3ac6-bbf1-6771e6a3df1b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor